<b>Question: When does an intentional action become habitual?</b> 
<p>
<b>Answer</b>: A desire for an outcome and a belief about a behavior that
leads to that outcome can result in an intention to perform that
behavior. When the intention is coupled with the skill to perform the
behavior and an awareness of performing it, the result is an
intentional action.  Such an action becomes habitual when frequent
repetition does not require the awareness component anymore.
