<b>Question</b>: We are a little unclear about what stereotype
vulnerability is - could you please clarify that for us?<p>

<b>Answer</b>: It's the vulnerability that a member of a stereotyped
group experiences when trying to achieve in a domain in which the
relevant stereotype implies low ability of that group (e.g., women in
math + science, African Americans in academics in general).  The
vulnerability itself leads to anxiety, distraction, and typically low
performance.
